  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN Ceasefire mediation course</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN Ceasefire mediation course (UNCFM) is an annual training in ceasefire mediation, planned and conducted in partnership between the UN DPPA&#x2019;s Mediation Support Unit, the Norwegian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Norwegian Defence International Centre (NODEFIC) and the Swiss Federal Department of Foreign Affairs. The training aims to engage mid- and senior-level officials of the United Nations and its partners who currently work in an environment where a ceasefire arrangement is either being mediated or already in place and who are directly involved in developing, supporting or management of a ceasefire or conflict reduction arrangements. Besides UN staff drawn from more than 23 UN field missions as well as HQs, the training is also attended by selected representatives from the some of the actual parties to conflict from across the world who bring realistic insights and rich experiences to the course.</narrative>
  </description>
